## File Naming and Organization

### Naming Conventions
- **Routes**: Use flat-routes convention with `+` for layout routes
- **Components**: PascalCase for component files (e.g., `UserProfile.tsx`)
- **Utilities**: kebab-case for utility files (e.g., `auth.server.ts`)
- **Tests**: Same name as file being tested with `.test.ts` suffix
- **Server files**: Use `.server.ts` suffix for server-only code

### Route Organization
Routes use the flat-routes convention:
- `_auth+/` - Layout routes (underscore prefix)
- `dashboard+/` - Nested route segments (plus suffix)
- `assessment+/` - **NEW** ESG assessment workflow routes
- `$username.tsx` - Dynamic route segments (dollar prefix)
- `users+/$username+/` - Nested dynamic routes
- `assessment.$id.tsx` - **NEW** Dynamic assessment detail routes

### Component Organization
- **UI components**: Place in `app/components/ui/` for reusable design system components
- **Feature components**: Place in `app/components/` for application-specific components
- **Assessment components**: Place in `app/components/assessment/` for ESG assessment features
- **Route components**: Colocate with routes when specific to a single route
- **Shared hooks**: Place in `app/components/hooks/` or `app/utils/`

## Database Schema

The application uses a comprehensive user management system with ESG assessment capabilities:
- **User model** - Core user data with relations
- **Authentication** - Multiple auth methods (password, OAuth, passkeys)
- **Authorization** - Role-based permissions system
- **Content** - Notes system with image attachments
- **Sessions** - Secure session management
- **Verification** - Email verification and TOTP
- **Assessments** - **NEW** ESG assessment data and answers

Key models:
- `User` - Central user entity with assessment relations
- `Password` - Bcrypt password storage
- `Session` - User sessions
- `Role` & `Permission` - RBAC system
- `Connection` - OAuth provider connections
- `Passkey` - WebAuthn credentials
- `Note` & `NoteImage` - Content management
- `Verification` - Email/TOTP verification
- `Assessment` - **NEW** ESG assessments with status and progress tracking
- `AssessmentAnswer` - **NEW** Individual question answers with metadata

### Assessment Models Detail

#### Assessment Model
```sql
model Assessment {
  id               String    @id @default(cuid())
  userId           String
  title            String?   // Optional assessment title
  status           String    @default("open") // open, completed, archived
  currentPageIndex Int       @default(0)
  surveyData       String    @default("{}") // JSON TEXT field
  createdAt        DateTime  @default(now())
  updatedAt        DateTime  @updatedAt
  completedAt      DateTime?
  
  user    User              @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  answers AssessmentAnswer[]
  
  @@index([userId])
  @@index([userId, status])
}
```

#### AssessmentAnswer Model
```sql
model AssessmentAnswer {
  id           String   @id @default(cuid())
  assessmentId String
  questionId   String   // unique question identifier
  questionName String   // SurveyJS question name
  section      String   // question section grouping
  answer       String   // JSON TEXT field for answer data
  createdAt    DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt    DateTime @updatedAt
  
  assessment Assessment @relation(fields: [assessmentId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  
  @@index([assessmentId])
  @@index([assessmentId, questionId])
  @@unique([assessmentId, questionId])
}
```

### Assessment Question Structure (v2.0 Enhancement)

The assessment system includes 88 ESG questions organized into 7 sections with enhanced help content structure:

- **SEZIONE 0**: Company identification (7 questions)
- **SEZIONE I**: Human rights commitment (19 questions)  
- **SEZIONE II**: Risk assessment (17 questions)
- **SEZIONE III**: Implementation measures (26 questions)
- **SEZIONE IV**: Monitoring (2 questions)
- **SEZIONE V**: Communication (11 questions)
- **SEZIONE VI**: Remediation (6 questions)

Each question includes:
- **Unique ID** and **Name** for SurveyJS integration
- **Italian text** with professional terminology
- **Question type** (radiogroup, text)
- **Standardized choices** for consistency
- **Enhanced help content structure (v2.0)**:
  - `help`: Contextual guidance for question understanding
  - `reporting`: Compliance and regulatory requirements
  - `docs`: Additional documentation and resources
- **Section grouping** for progress tracking
- **Markdown support** in titles and help content
- **Field name display** for better context

